<p>At the heart of it, this is a flawed article. There are some pretty glaring SPaG issues and formatting quirks that were major enough to detract from my ability to read the article. The most notable of those is the placement of lines in the exploration log right next to each other without breaks, which causes a wall of text appearance that's hard to read.</p>
<p>The dialogue is also a weak point, and there were a few pieces of dialogue that I disliked. It was a bit hard to follow the dialogue at points, particularly at the end of the second exploration log, where I read it a few times but still wasn't sure of what was happening.</p>
<p>However, I did still enjoy this despite the flaws. I read through to the end, despite a lot of the above flaws being enough to make me stop reading in most. It's a nice atmospheric article, and when I was able to follow the action it was engaging. Although it could be improved, I did like this enough to upvote.</p>

